   "spoken": "In the King's Indian, Black strikes with c5, challenging White's centre and opening lines for the fianchettoed bishop — refusing to sit passively against White's quiet setup.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Meet a slow White system by striking the centre with c5.",
   "plans": "Follow with Qa5 pressure and watch the c3-knight."
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
